Ticket [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merges reports for two different date problems. The export
contains overlapping rows, so the table counts each report ID once before grouping by the
tenant's locale and booking form.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Shared parser reads month first

For day-first tenant locales, the shared parser still reads month first. This cause appears
across app, email, and form reports. The desk also flagged one-day-move reports; classified by
tenant locale, they remain in this group.

Track the parser fix in [GitHub issue #2](https://github.com/michalczyz42/what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Booking-v3 hint conflicts with tenant locale

Booking-v3 displays `MM/DD/YYYY`, but these tenants use day-first locales. People follow the
hint while the form interprets the date in the tenant's order, producing a separate mismatch.

Track the form hint and parsing fix in [GitHub issue #1](https://github.com/michalczyz42/what-it-shows/issues/1).

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not merge these groups by subject or intake tag alone. Resolve the cause using the tenant's
locale and booking form, and count each report ID once.
</Callout>

